  "steps": [
    "Pat the chicken thighs dry with paper towels and season both sides evenly with salt and black pepper.",
    "In a small bowl, whisk together the honey, soy sauce, minced garlic, grated ginger, and apple cider vinegar until well combined.",
    "Heat the olive oil in a 12-inch skillet over medium-high heat. Once the oil is shimmering, add the chicken thighs in a single layer.",
    "Cook the chicken for 5-7 minutes per side until the exterior is deeply browned and the internal temperature reaches 165°F (74°C).",
    "Reduce the heat to medium and pour the honey garlic sauce into the skillet. Let the sauce simmer for 2-3 minutes, spooning it over the chicken frequently, until the glaze is thick and sticky.",
    "Remove from heat and garnish with sliced green onions before serving."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "For extra heat, add a teaspoon of red pepper flakes or sriracha to the sauce whisking step.",
    "Ensure the pan is hot before adding the chicken to get a proper sear and prevent sticking.",
    "If the sauce thickens too quickly, add a splash of water or chicken broth to loosen it."
  ],
  "storage": "Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 4 days. Reheat in a skillet over low heat with a splash of water.",
